From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] smb: client: release the NLS reference when mounting fails

cifs_setup_cifs_sb() takes a reference to the mount's NLS table before
cifs_mount() authenticates. If authentication or tree connection fails,
the out path frees cifs_sb without reaching delayed_free(), leaking the
NLS reference. Repeated bad passwords therefore pin nls_utf8 indefinitely.

Balance the reference on this failure path as delayed_free() does on
normal unmount. The zero-initialized pointer is safe on earlier failures.

Signed-off-by: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
---
 fs/smb/client/cifsfs.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/smb/client/cifsfs.c b/fs/smb/client/cifsfs.c
--- a/fs/smb/client/cifsfs.c
+++ b/fs/smb/client/cifsfs.c
@@ -1088,6 +1088,7 @@ cifs_smb3_do_mount(struct fs_context *fc, struct smb3_fs_context *old_ctx)
 	deactivate_locked_super(sb);
 	return root;
 out:
+	unload_nls(cifs_sb->local_nls);
 	kfree(cifs_sb->prepath);
 	smb3_cleanup_fs_context(cifs_sb->ctx);
 	kfree(cifs_sb);

